  "worked_solution": "Let the function $f(x,y)$ be defined as\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=2x-y+3.\n$$\n\nThe function $f(x,y)$ is continuous for all values of $x$ and $y.$ So, we can calculate the limit by substituting $(-2,0)$ into the function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (-2,0)}(2x-y+3) & =2(-2)-0+3 \\\\  & =-4-0+3 \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$",
